ry."}, {"sourceSlug": "globalization", "sourceName": "Globalization", "verb": "TRANSFORMS", "targetSlug": "escp-business-school", "targetName": "ESCP Business School", "context": "The forces of globalization have transformed ESCP's programs to focus on international business since the turn of the 21st century."}], "places": [{"name": "Paris, France", "role": "Birthplace"}, {"name": "London, United Kingdom", "role": "Campus"}, {"name": "Berlin, Germany", "role": "Campus"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: ESCP Business School", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "escp-business-school"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q29293", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ESCP_Business_School"], "tags": ["Germany", "business school", "Europe", "Law Schools & Legal Academies", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "ESCP Business School left a notable mark on Modern history, documented across 56 Wikipedia editions worldwide. Key lasting impacts include: Shaped institutional landscape and community development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "ESCP Business School has played a pivotal role in shaping business education in Europe, influencing thousands of students and producing notable alumni who have led major corporations and innovations. Its establishment and evolution reflect broader economic and educational transformations in the 19th and 20th centuries.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-02T20:56:39Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28620725752", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Business school in paris, france. ESCP Business School is a business school in 11th arrondissement of Paris, established in 1819-12-01. Holds notable historical significance, documented across 56 language editions of Wikipedia. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "ESCP Business School, established on December 1, 1819, in the 11th arrondissement of Paris, France, is one of the world's oldest business schools and is recognized for its pioneering role in business education. It was founded by a group of entrepreneurs and educators led by the visionary Henri de Villeneuve-Bargemont, who sought to create an institution that would meet the growing demand for formal business training in the wake of the Industrial Revolution. Over the years, ESCP has expanded its reach across Europe, with campuses in London, Berlin, Madrid, Turin, and Warsaw, thus making its influence felt in the broader context of international business education.

Throughout its history, ESCP has made significant contributions to the development of business curricula and practices. The school introduced innovative teaching methods and a unique pedagogy that combined theoretical knowledge with practical application, which became a model for other institutions. By the late 19th century, ESCP developed a strong reputation, leading to a network of alumni who would go on to impact various sectors, from finance to technology. In 1973, it became the first business school to establish an international curriculum, further solidifying its role as a leader in global business education.

